## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-tenant design under privacy, governance, and ops constraints typical at large platforms, plus data residency and cost visibility.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant feature stores and private endpoints for isolation
- Privacy-preserving cross-tenant aggregation (secure aggregation + DP-SGD)
- Canary rollout and multi-region deployment for safe updates
- Data provenance with BigQuery Data Catalog and lineage tracking
- Per-tenant cost controls and explicit rollback criteria
- Data residency considerations (EU vs US tenants)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: privacy-preserving cross-tenant gradient aggregation
function aggregateCrossTenantGradients(grads, epsilon, delta) {
  // clip per-example gradients, add Gaussian noise, sum and normalize
  const clipped = grads.map(g => clip(g, 1.0));
  const sum = clipped.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
  const noise = gaussianNoise(epsilon, delta, sum.length);
  return (sum + noise) / grads.length;
}
```

